-whereas the group 1h hydrogenase and form-I carbon monoxide dehydrogenase were retained. Root-adjacent
-communities were enriched in faster-growing genomes, and the 1l loss was smaller at greener sites,
-but these proxies of plant carbon explained a minor part of the loss: carrying group 1l predicted
-the depletion of a genus beside roots beyond its predicted growth rate and phylum. Across sites,
